# SPRINT 11: Secure MMIO Boot Sequencer
#
# Scenario: Privilege-separated peripheral initialization
#
# A boot ROM must initialize three hardware peripherals in order:
#
#   1. Boot status register (0x30, Siddha, Ring2)
#      Write initial status flags to the shared status bus.
#      Globally visible -- any process can read it.
#
#   2. Clock control register (0x50, Asiddha, Ring0)
#      Configure the PLL. Isolated register -- kernel access only.
#      Must be inside a privileged scope.
#
#   3. Security lock register (0x60, Asiddha, Ring0) -- SANDHI-FUSED with above
#      Write config, then atomically lock it.
#      The write-then-lock pair must be atomic: if any instruction executes
#      between them, the lock can be bypassed by a race condition.
#      Sandhi makes this an explicit, compile-time-verified atomic pair.
#
#   4. Boot status confirm (0x30, Siddha, Ring2)
#      Signal that initialization is complete.
#
# Bug class prevented:
#   In unstructured firmware (C, assembly), three classes of bugs are common:
#
#   BUG-1: Unscoped privileged write
#     A Ring0 MMIO write outside any privilege scope is invisible to auditors.
#     P4 prevents this structurally -- Ring0 without अधिकारः cannot compile.
#
#   BUG-2: Privileged write to shared bus
#     Writing with Ring0 authority to a globally visible (Siddha) address
#     conflates kernel privilege with user-visible state.
#     P3 prevents this -- Ring0 on addr < 0x50 cannot compile.
#
#   BUG-3: Non-atomic configure-then-lock
#     If the security register write and lock are not executed atomically,
#     a cycle-timing adversary can insert a write between them.
#     Sandhi prevents this -- the pair is declared atomic at compile time,
#     FLAGS=0xE in the binary signals the firmware to execute it atomically.
#
# ABI words expected:
#   0x200530F0  Write  boot_status  (Ring2, Siddha, standalone)
#   0x00AA00F0  ADHIKARA_OPEN
#   0x00CC50F0  Store  clock_ctrl   (Ring0, Asiddha, inside scope)
#   0x00CC60E0  Store  sec_lock     (Ring0, Asiddha, SANDHI-FIRST)
#   0x00CC60F0  Store  sec_lock     (Ring0, Asiddha, SANDHI-PAIR -- atomic with above)
#   0x00BB00F0  ADHIKARA_CLOSE
#   0x200530F0  Write  boot_status  (Ring2, Siddha, confirm)
#
# Expected UART:
#   status_writes=0x02  privileged_inits=0x01  clock_stores=0x01
#   lock_stores=0x02  sandhi_pairs=0x01  scope_opens=0x01  scope_closes=0x01

सञ्ज्ञा घड़ी = 0x50 ।
सञ्ज्ञा सुरक्षा = 0x60 ।

तन्त्रशास्त्रम् {
    # 1. Signal boot start (Ring2, shared status bus)
    वाचम् लिखति ।

    # 2-3. Enter privileged scope: configure clock, then atomically write+lock security reg
    अधिकारः {
        घड़ी स्थापयति ।        # Clock PLL config (Ring0, isolated)
        सुरक्षा स्थापयति ।     # Security reg write  (Ring0, isolated, SANDHI-FIRST)
        सन्धिः ।
        सुरक्षा स्थापयति ।     # Security reg lock   (Ring0, isolated, atomic pair)
    }

    # 4. Signal boot complete (Ring2, shared status bus)
    वाचम् लिखति ।
}
